{
  "dom_id": "step-q222359",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "The minimum value of the function $y=|x+1|+3$ is $y=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that $y=|x-h|+k$ is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $h$ units right and $k$ units up.\n\nThe function $y=|x+1|+3$ has $h=-1$ and $k=3.$ Therefore, it is a translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $1$ unit *left* and $3$ units *up*.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192632/assets/aabce12b2665678053ad7a440be44dc0b73e37d2ab45664a2347f55c14641b2a.png)\n\nLooking at the graph, we can see that the minimum value of $y$ is $3.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
